The descent audit now has a concrete obstruction: an explicit joint positive-definite profile system saturates the Bessel budget while losing the `[0,1]` pattern bound. Positivity and Bessel alone therefore cannot justify the next descent step. I’ve also stated one uniform capture inequality that would complete the argument via P40. It survived the finite tests across all five requested families, but remains conjectural.
